   "id": "q1",
   "title": "How do we apply a median filter to a 3×3 matrix?",
   "body": "I get the idea of sorting neighbours but I am not sure what happens at the borders.",
   "subject": "Image Processing",
   "topic": "Spatial filters",
   "by": "u5",
   "when": "2 days ago",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": "a1",
     "by": "u2",
     "text": "Collect the 9 values in the window, sort them and take the middle one (the 5th). Replace the centre pixel with it. At borders, pad the image by replicating edge pixels, or skip border pixels.",
     "votes": 7,
     "accepted": true,
     "verified": true
    },
    {
     "id": "a2",
     "by": "u6",
     "text": "Same as the averaging filter but you use the median instead of the mean, which is why it removes salt-and-pepper noise well.",
     "votes": 3,
     "accepted": false,
     "verified": false
    }
   ]
  },
